From c743ee8235c2ab974014297b7e54aa563c13e3ad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mesa-nvk-horizon <mesa-nvk-horizon@localhost>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 14:47:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 27/30] nouveau/vk: nvkmd_horizon, declare GPU_MULTI_WAIT on
 the sync type
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

vk_sync_timeline requires VK_SYNC_FEATURE_GPU_MULTI_WAIT of the type it
is built on (vk_sync_timeline.c:51-60), and vk_sync.c:74 requires
GPU_WAIT alongside it. Both are asserts, so omitting it was silent in
an NDEBUG build and an abort inside vkCreateDevice in a debug one — the
sync type registered for timeline emulation did not meet the contract
of the thing emulating over it.

It is also simply true. nvkmd_horizon_ctx_wait takes a wait_count and
waits on every entry, so more than one sync in a submit is a case it
already handles; the declaration was describing less than the code does.

mesa-nvk-horizon: Phase 4 — audit before the next hardware run
Why: found by reading vk_sync_timeline_type_validate() while checking
  what vkCreateDevice does after the point the second console run
  reached.
Evidence: mesa/src/vulkan/runtime/vk_sync_timeline.c:51-60 and
  vk_sync.c:60-75. No runtime behaviour changes in this build; every
  use of the flag is an assert.
Upstream: no — this is the Horizon backend's own sync type.
---
 .../vulkan/nvkmd/horizon/nvkmd_horizon_sync.c        | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvkmd/horizon/nvkmd_horizon_sync.c b/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvkmd/horizon/nvkmd_horizon_sync.c
index ed91d75..3d226f9 100644
--- a/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvkmd/horizon/nvkmd_horizon_sync.c
+++ b/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvkmd/horizon/nvkmd_horizon_sync.c
@@ -199,6 +199,18 @@ const struct vk_sync_type nvk_horizon_sync_type = {
    .size = sizeof(struct nvk_horizon_sync),
    .features = VK_SYNC_FEATURE_BINARY |
                VK_SYNC_FEATURE_GPU_WAIT |
+               /* The runtime's timeline emulation requires this of the
+                * type it is built on (vk_sync_timeline.c:51-60), and
+                * vk_sync.c:74 requires GPU_WAIT alongside it. Both
+                * checks are asserts, so leaving it out was silent in
+                * this NDEBUG build and an abort in vkCreateDevice in a
+                * debug one.
+                *
+                * It is also true: nvkmd_horizon_ctx_wait takes a
+                * wait_count and waits on every entry, so more than one
+                * sync in a submit is a case it already handles.
+                */
+               VK_SYNC_FEATURE_GPU_MULTI_WAIT |
                VK_SYNC_FEATURE_CPU_WAIT |
                VK_SYNC_FEATURE_CPU_RESET |
                VK_SYNC_FEATURE_CPU_SIGNAL |
